{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0005789","label":"hepatitis D virus infection","definition":"Inflammation of the liver in humans caused by hepatitis delta virus, a defective RNA virus that can only infect hepatitis B patients. For its viral coating, hepatitis delta virus requires the hepatitis B surface antigens produced by these patients. Hepatitis D can occur either concomitantly with (coinfection) or subsequent to (superinfection) hepatitis B infection. Similar to hepatitis B, it is primarily transmitted by parenteral exposure, such as transfusion of contaminated blood or blood products, but can also be transmitted via sexual or intimate personal contact.","synonyms":["HDV","Hepatitis D","Hepatitis D virus","Hepatitis delta virus caused hepatitis","Hepatitis delta virus hepatitis","hepatitis delta","hepatitis type D"],"xrefs":["DOID:2047","EFO:0007304","GARD:0021716","ICD9:070.52","MEDGEN:4182","MESH:D003699","NORD:2020","Orphanet:402823","SCTID:707341005","UMLS:C0011226"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":3,"is_group":false,"n_genes":0,"n_phenotypes":18,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[],"phenotypes":[{"edge":{"id":"e_8ff50d81c296","source":"MONDO:0005789","target":"HP:0031964","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:402823 · ORPHA:402823","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/402823","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.6,"snippet":"Hepatitis delta: Elevated circulating alanine aminotransferase concentration (frequency HP:0040282) [TAS]"},{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:402823","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/402823","confidence":0.6,"snippet":"Elevated circulating alanine aminotransferase concentration — Frequent (79-30%)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.6,"independent_sources":["Orphanet"],"level":"curated"},"phenotype":{"id":"HP:0031964","label":"Elevated circulat